{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/856605-sidereals-stupid-dice-tricks","id":856605,"title":"Sidereals - Stupid Dice Tricks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-31T11:09:35-07:00","id":856605,"title":"Sidereals - Stupid Dice Tricks","content":"Sidereals can raise their opponent's TN. None of their QC charms provide Double X, Reroll X or Explode X.<br /> <br /> Double X and Explode X successes increases variance. Reroll X failures decreases variance.<br /> <br /> I don't anticipate Sidereals dipping heavily into reroll X failures; their variance control is already the best in the game. To the extent that they do, I expect it will be, like the Terrestrial Excellency, limited to only (Essence) dice.<br /> <br /> Double and Explode increase the number of expected successes but also increase variance is something I could see- but with such strong TN control, the variance won't change by as much as it would normally, making them closer to just another indirect TN enhancer. Perhaps a smattering of Double 9s, or something like Triple 10s, but more as an accent than a common element.<br /> <br /> I expect that the Sidereals will have some of the more 'weird' or esoteric stupid dice tricks- finding matched sets, finding runs, that sort of thing- but probably not in combat charms. Those need to be as fast as possible to resolve, and the combat itself is providing the tension / interest, as opposed to dice rolls during extended actions like crafting.<br /> <br /> What Sidereals need (as far as stupid dice tricks are concerned) are ways to increase successes at the cost of meaningfully increasing variance.<br /> <br /> Basically, gambling is fun, and Sidereals need a means to gamble. Granted, they also need a way to rig the game, but they should be able to gamble honestly too, and in such a way that they can't benefit from both at once.<br /> <br /> They could also have re-roll effects that are 'punitive' for reducing the TN. 'You may re-roll 5s until no 5s appear. Rerolled successes are not added to your total number of successes' diminishes the value of TN reduction to 4 or 5; depending on the cost of the charm or what other benefits it provides anyways.<br /> <br /> *brainstorms*<br /> <br /> * Roll at least half of your dice. If you get X successes or fewer, the remaining dice all come up as successes; otherwise, they all come up as failures.<br /> * Gain (Bonus) for each die that equals (target); do not count successes added by those dice.<br /> * Gain (Bonus) for each failure you roll. (Eg: Add the number of failures on this roll to your raw damage when you make a withering attack.)<br /> * Push Your Luck Explosions: You may re-roll any number of successes, accumulating successes with each reroll. If you roll no successes, all accumulated successes are lost. (Too good and too fiddly for combat. Save for crafting)<br /> * Trade two failures for one success on a roll (at a fixed cost before the roll; there would certainly be a breakpoint where it becomes obviously better or worse. Have to math)<br /> * Swap number of failures for number of successes. (Again, would need to be a fixed cost, but less likely to have an obvious breakpoint. Might be usable after the roll but would need either a once-per-scene limit or other strong inhibitor)<br /> <br /> I suspect that Gain (Bonus) for each failure you roll is going to prove to be a relatively rich space to mine- Solars have a little in that area, like the Socialize charm that lets you throw your 1s and 2s at someone else. The tricky thing will be ensuring that outright failure doesn't become more attractive than success, as that's just another kind of variance control.<br /> <br /> And this isn't discounting the other more straight up TN toys that can exist- reduce TN to 5 if Major Intimacy or 4 if Defining Intimacy, that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:21:07-07:00","id":856686,"title":"","content":"I'm expecting them to be good at punishing people for rolling 1s. Making enemies unlucky seems like a fate ninja kind of thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:28:05-07:00","id":856687,"title":"","content":"Re: Sanctaphrax; this has the nice thematic synergy of &quot;My tricks and schemes don't work on him!&quot; against Solars with the semi-ubiquitous &quot;Reroll all my 1s, bitches&quot; charms. In this way, the Solar has a huge advantage against the Sidereal <i>without </i>needing stupidly overpowered charms / the Sidereal to have uselessly weak charms. Which I like; the difference between the two approaching a third party [a behemoth or demon] is far closer to Mastery vs Normal MA, while head-on against each other, the Solar's edge shines brightly because he has no flaws to capitalize on.<br /> <br /> This is far preferable to the 2e &quot;non-Solar charms are like Solar charms with half or more of their limbs amputated&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:07:06-07:00","id":856709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/856605-sidereals-stupid-dice-tricks?p=856686#post856686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm expecting them to be good at punishing people for rolling 1s. Making enemies unlucky seems like a fate ninja kind of thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent thought!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}